><surname>Campagna</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnbom</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Genetic and morphometric differentiation between island and mainland southern elephant seal populations.</article-title><source>Proc Roy Soc B</source><volume>268</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>332</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000554-Bandelt1"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bandelt</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Forster</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rohl</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Median-joining networks for inferring intraspecific phylogenies.</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10331250</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000554-Drummond1"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Drummond</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rambaut</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>BEAST: Bayesian evolutionary analysis by sampling trees.</article-title><source>BMC Evol Biol</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>214</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17996036</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000554-Rambaut1"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rambaut</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>SYW</given-names></name><name><surname>Drummond</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Shapiro</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Accommodating the effects of ancient DNA damage on inferences of demographic histories.</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>248</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19001634</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000554-Ho1"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>SYW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolokotronis</surname><given-names>S-O</given-names></name><name><surname>Allaby</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Elevated substitution rates estimated from ancient DNA sequences.</article-title><source>Biol Letters</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>702</fpage><lpage>705</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000554-Lambert1"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ritchie</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Millar</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Holland</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Drummond</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Rates of evolution in ancient DNA from Ad&#x000e9;lie penguins.</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>295</volume><fpage>2270</fpage><lpage>2273</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11910113</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000554-Howell1"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Howell</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Smejkal</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mackey</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chinnery</surname><given-names>PF</given-names></name><name><surname>Turnbull</surname><give